-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",17,{
[513]="7006AA33\n1\tFind the meeting place in Tâkhdar; the Cellars\tTravelling separately, Belondor has asked you to meet Tabrím and himself in Umbar-môkh at a place in Tâkhdar; the Cellars, east of Tilmakhím.\n2\tTalk to Belondor in Umbar-môkh\tYou have arrived in Umbar-môkh, where you are to join Belondor in meeting with Tabrím. You should talk to Belondor.\n3\tTalk to Tabrím\tYou have arrived in Umbar-môkh, where you have joined Belondor and Tabrím. You should see what Tabrím has to say.\n4\tTalk to Belondor\tTabrím has revealed that the Order of the Eagle knows that Azagath and Nakási were preparing to travel by land, not by sea. He put forth the Order's theory that the two went to Mâkhda Khorbo to retrieve something. Identifying what that was should help reveal their destination. You should talk to Belondor.\n",
[514]="7006AA40\n1\tTalk to Belondor in Umbar-môkh; the Neaths\tBelondor is ready to face his fears and return to Mâkhda Khorbo. He has asked you to accompany him. You should talk to him when you are ready.\n2\tTalk to Belondor in Dâr Laja\tAfter returning to Mâkhda Khorbo with Belondor, you discovered that Azagath and Nakási took from the temple a map of inland areas east of Umbar. You should talk to Belondor in Dâr Laja, the Meeting-hall.\n",
[515]="7000978F\n1\tTalk to Elrond\tElrond is in the library on the top floor of the Last Homely House. Aragorn told you to bring a message to Master Elrond, with assurances that the Elf-lord will understand his words. The message Aragorn told you to speak is this: 'I know now what Gwindeth sought of me in the watery darkness, and I am prepared to give it. Elendil was a wiser man than I.'\n",
[516]="7005314E\n1\tInvestigate Sharkey's Slough\tSharkey's Slough can be found in the centre of the Gladden Fields. Through the help of his friend, Radagast has asked you to investigate Sharkey's Slough in the Gladden Fields and learn what became of the remnants of Saruman's forces in his absence.\n2\tSigns of the White Hand can be found at Sharkey's Slough in the Gladden Fields. Fearing that Sharkey has driven out the remnants of the White Hand, Radagast has asked you to search for signs of Saruman's forces at Sharkey's Slough.\t\n3\tFind the leader of the forces at Sharkey's Slough\tThe leader of Sharkey's Men at Sharkey's Slough might be found in the dredging pit. It seems Sharkey's Men have driven out or slain many of the White Hand forces that remained in the Vales of Anduin. You should search for their leader and attempt to disrupt whatever plans Sharkey has for the Gladden Fields.\n4\tThe slain Shakh-hai can be found in the dredging pit at the centre of Sharkey's Slough. You have found what appears to be the one-time leader of the White Hand forces in the Gladden Fields. You should examine the Shakh-hai's remains.\t\n5\tExamine 'Sharkey's Orders'\tSharkey's lieutenant was in possession of a missive containing Sharkey's orders. You should examine Sharkey's orders and see if they reveal more of Sharkey's plans for the Gladden Fields. NOTE: 'Sharkey's Orders' must be used in your inventory and you must accept the quest 'Dredging up the Past' to complete this quest.\n",
[517]="70028E4A\n1\tCollect iridescent crow-feathers (total: 12)\tIridescent crow-feathers can be found in plenty on Rook's trained crebain. You should collect iridescent feathers from Rook's craban-flock.\n2\tCraft an iridescent cloak\tA weaver's loom can be found near Rook's Hut. You should use the weaver's loom to weave the feathers into an iridescent cloak.\n3\tBring the many-coloured cloak you crafted to Rook\tRook is at his hut in Pren Gwydh. You should bring the iridescent, many-hued cloak you crafted to Rook, who wishes to be as great a Wizard as Saruman.\n",
[518]="7007251D\n1\tValukhâri sent you to the library to find the Doorward's map of Mûr Ghala. You should go there and compare the map provided by Bêtam.\t\n2\tReturn to Valukhâri at her post in Zajâna\tAfter comparing the maps, it is clear the map the Doorwards crafted is missing a section to the far south-east of Adagím. You should return to Valukhâri and ask her about this.\n",
[519]="7002B5B8\n1\tItems from the market list can be found throughout Bywater during the Farmers Faire. The market list is in your inventory. You should collect the items on the market list...but avoid collecting items that are not listed. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\t\n2\tBring the goods to Daisy Sandyman\tDaisy Sandyman is at the market stall at the Farmers Faire. You should bring the goods you collected to Daisy Sandyman.\n",
[520]="70062DE1\n1\tDefeat Orcs in Tharbad (total: 10)\030Find Huel's missing axe somewhere in Tharbad\tHuel asked you to defeat some of the Orcs that prowl now within Tharbad, and to recover the axe he left behind if you can find it.\n2\tBring the axe you recovered to Woodcutter Huel just inside the southern entrance to Tharbad\tWoodcutter Huel is just inside the southern entrance of Tharbad.\n",
[521]="70058BBC\n1\tDefeat Narg-and-Mauz\tNarg-and-Mauz can be found deep within Bagûd-mekhem. Náin has commanded you to defeat Narg-and-Mauz, the powerful two-headed troll that leads the forces at Bagûd-mekhem.\n2\tTalk to Náin at Drenghól\tNáin the Slakeless can be found at Drenghól in the War of Three Peaks. You have defeated Narg-and-Mauz. You should report to Náin with news of this victory.\n",
[522]="7001A496\n1\tDefeat Lebrennil\tThe spider-nest lies near the Willow Glade, to the south of Gillemin's old camp. Gillemin warned that you should be wary of a matron within the spider-nest.\n2\tTalk to Gillemin Brandybuck in the Old Forest\tGillemin Brandybuck awaits you at his new camp, south-east of Old Muddyfoot's Hill. You should return to Gillemin Brandybuck with news of your success.\n",
[523]="7002C699\n1\tFind a clue to the shade-captain's whereabouts\tThe Oathbreaker captain lurks among his men atop the hill to the west. Idmar has asked you to find the captain of the shades.\n2\tDefeat the shade-captain's defenders (total: 2)\tThe Oathbreaker captain's men have sprung forth to guard him. They must be defeated if you are to continue your charge.\n3\tExamine the skull\tA peculiar skull is impaled on a nearby tree...perhaps this is the key to drawing the Oathbreaker captain forth.\n4\tTalk to the shade-captain\tThe Oathbreaker captain is atop the hill to the west of Idmar's camp. You should attempt to speak to him now that he has revealed himself.\n",
[524]="70020BC6\n1\tBring ox-meat to the Uch-lûth oxherds at Uch Cadlus\tThe oxherds of the Uch-lûth are encamped at Uch Cadlus, south-east of Echad Saeradan. Andreg has asked you to deliver the ox-meat you collected to the oxherds of the Uch-lûth.\n",
[525]="7000758B\n1\tBring the boar-heads to Roger Hawkling\030Collect boar-heads (total: 10)\tBoars range the wilds around Adso's camp and are strewn throughout the southern Bree-fields. Roger wants you to thin the growing number of wild boars and bring him their heads. He cooks an amazing delicacy from them.\n",
[526]="70020C35\n1\tBring the ox-meat to Andreg at Echad Saeradan\tAndreg is at Echad Saeradan in the Windfells of Enedwaith, north-west of Uch Cadlus. Wunne has asked you to deliver a package of meat to the Grey Company.\n2\tTalk to Wunne at Uch Cadlus\tWunne is at Uch Cadlus in the Windfells, south-east of Echad Saeradan. Andreg instructed you to return to Wunne and offer her your services should she need them again.\n",
[527]="700173CF\n1\tCollect books of Tham Mírdain (total: 12)\tThe Library of Tham Mírdain is south and a little west of Echad Mirobel. As you work towards cleansing the Library of Tham Mírdain, you should keep a watchful eye for any tomes which may still be intact.\n",
[528]="70044293\n1\tTalk to Mithrandir in the Citadel and travel with him to the Old Archives\tMithrandir is in the Court of the Fountain, in the Citadel atop the city. Mithrandir is waiting to walk with you to the Old Archives, where he wants to learn what befell you in Osgiliath.\n2\tTalk to Mithrandir in the Citadel atop the city\tMithrandir is in the Citadel atop the city. You have returned from the Old Archives with Mithrandir, and he has obtained your vow of silence concerning Gothmog's lineage.\n",
[529]="70047BE1\n1\tReturn to Haerondir with Artamir's warning\tHaerondir can be found to the south of Ondoher's Folly in Dagorlad. You have learned much from the spirit of Faramir and should now deliver a warning to the Host of the West at Haerondir.\n2\tTalk to Laeglaw at Haerondir\tLaeglaw can be found in Haerondir. You have returned to Haerondir and have been spotted by Laeglaw and Mincham. You should speak to Laeglaw.\n3\tTalk to Anborn at Haerondir\tAnborn can be found at Haerondir. You have returned to Haerondir too late, and now Laeglaw fears Anborn has sent his men on a foolish errand. You should speak to Anborn and ask what you can do to aid him.\n",
[530]="7000758A\n1\tBring the bear-pelts to Roger Hawkling\030Collect bear-pelts (total: 10)\tBears can be found throughout the southern Bree-fields, but a sizable sloth of bears can be found north of Outlaw's Haven found west and north of Adso's Camp. Roger Hawkling has asked you to hunt some bears and bring him their pelts.\n",
[531]="70066C2A\n1\tBring the letter to Byrski Hardprow at Mekhem-bizru, in the Dimrill Dale\tByrski Hardprow sent you a letter requesting that you visit him in the Dimrill Dale. Deliver the letter to Byrski Hardprow. He can be found at Mekhem-bizru in the Dimrill Dale.\n",
[532]="7004A8E3\n1\tBurn crates of distasteful rations in Kála-murg (total: 8)\tCrates of distasteful rations can be found through Kála-murg in Rath Cail. You have discovered crates filled with disgusting rations in Kála-murg. You should burn them in case they are the cause of \"the hollowing.\"\n2\tCompleted\tYou have burned many crates of distasteful rations in Kála-murg.\n",
[533]="7000016F\n1\tBring the bear and boar meat to Ella Lilypond in Newbury\030Collect bear-haunches (total: 8)\030Collect boar-shanks (total: 8)\tSuitable boars and bears can be found north of Buckland, between the Brandy Hills and the borders of the Old Forest. Ella Lilypond waits in Newbury just beyond the gates of Buckland. Ella Lilypond is collecting meat to support Adso's inn. The meat is to create food that will make Men travelling the Great East Road feel more welcome and at home.\n",
[534]="700544A7\n1\tDestroy Morgul blades (total: 12)\tMorgul blades can be found in the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul. You should destroy any Morgul blades that you find.\n2\tTalk to Dolenthol in Barad Orhant\tDolenthol can be found in Barad Orhant. You should talk to Dolenthol.\n",
[535]="70066880\n1\tTalk to Húrwen\tLúmar is concerned that his fellow scout hasn't reported back after making a trip north of Iáphel. Igerna was last seen heading to Elbery Farm in Pinnath Gelin, to speak with Húrwen. You should speak with Húrwen.\n2\tSearch for Igerna\tHúrwen spoke with Igerna, who continued on towards the mountains in search of more goblins. You should look for signs of Igerna in northern Pinnath Gelin.\n3\tSearch the camp for Igerna\tWhile searching for Igerna, you discovered that goblins have made a camp at the foot of the mountains. You should continue looking for Igerna in the goblin camp in north-western Pinnath Gelin.\n4\tSearch the cave for Igerna\tA freshly made cave has been blasted into the mountainside by goblins. You should search the cave. The cave is in north-western Pinnath Gelin.\n5\tTalk to Lúmar in Ost Arndír\tIn a newly dug cave north of Iáphel, you found a shredded pack. Does it belong to Igerna? You should bring it to Lúmar in Ost Arndir to find out.\n",
[536]="700097DF\n1\tTalk to Gwindeth\tThe Blue Lady lives at Gwindethrond, a cave behind the waterfall at Rushingdale in the hills of western Emyn Uial on the far side of the lake, west and slightly south of Tinnudir and Tyl Ruinen. Calenglad has arranged a meeting with Gwindeth and warned you to speak to her with respect and honesty. Only Gwindeth can grant you access to the Silithar needed by Aragorn.\n",
[537]="7000E8FF\n1\tCollect Bombur's Beard Lager from Thorin's Hall\tThorin's Hall is in Ered Luin, far to the west of the North Downs. You should purchase some Bombur's Beard Lager from the barkeep in the basement of Thorin's Hall.\n2\tBring Bombur's Beard Lager to Múli\tMúli is at Othrikar in the North Downs, far to the east of Ered Luin. Múli has asked you to bring him some \"Bombur's Beard Lager\" from Thorin's Hall. Once you have the beer, you should bring it back to Múli in Othrikar.\n",
[538]="70062E2A\n1\tFree captured hobbits (total: 6)\tRadlaw can be found to the north of Clegur. The humble merchant has asked you to free his friends.\n2\tTalk to the humble merchant in Clegur\tThe hobbits have been released. The humble merchant should hear about this.\n",
[539]="7002CB78\n1\tRead the message that was left for you\tThe message has been left for you near Landroval at his clearing in the north. Someone has left you a letter, which you may open and read.\n2\tTalk to Landroval\030Talk to Meneldor\tLandroval and Meneldor can be found at the clearing of trees in the north-east section of Wailing Hills. Landroval and Meneldor wish to speak with you once more, before you depart for Stangard.\n3\tTalk to Sabert at the north-eastern gate of Stangard\tSabert guards the north-eastern entrance to Stangard, in Eorlsmead. Sabert wishes to speak with you about the events that have transpired in Stangard during your absence.\n",
[540]="70069DF4\n1\tFind the Ranger keeping watch outside of Tornhad\tYou should look for a Ranger outside of Tornhad who is keeping watch, to whom you should deliver the letter. Tornhad is in the southern region of the Angle of Mitheithel.\n2\tTalk to the Ranger keeping watch\tYou have found the Ranger Calithil, who is keeping watch outside of Tornhad. You should talk to him and give him the letter.\n",
[541]="70028189\n1\tDestroy Dievlig standard (total: 4)\030Defeat Sawul\tThe hill where Bledhun's party was once encamped lies to the south of Bledhun's current camp. Bledhun asked you to seek out and destroy any standards that you find at his old encampment and defeat the captains that took the hill.\n2\tTalk to Bledhun at his encampment in the Bonevales\tBledhun is at his encampment, south of the hill where his party formerly encamped. You should return to Bledhun and inform him that you were able to destroy the standards that littered the camp and defeated the captains that you encountered.\n",
[542]="7002CA5E\n1\tTalk to Cabed\tCabed is near Ost Celebrant, on a small hill off the side of the road south. Doron has sent you to find the lost messenger, Cabed.\n",
[543]="7002FDC6\n1\tFind and talk to Fastred\tFastred can be found inside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn. After arriving in Snowbourn, Gísling wants you to speak with Fastred, Reeve of the Sutcrofts, about the perils facing his people.\n2\tTalk to Léofhelm\tLéofhelm is inside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn. Fastred is nowhere to be found. Perhaps one of his men will know of his whereabouts.\n",
[544]="7004A8E8\n1\tTalk to Belzagar in the Tower of Cirith Ungol\tBelzagar can be found in the turret of the Tower of Cirith Ungol. Legolas has asked you to attempt to convey his message of warning to Belzagar to again reinforce the Tower of Cirith Ungol.\n2\tScrawl a message of warning to the Gúrzyul in Belzagar's book\tBelzagar's book can be found near him in the turret of the Tower of Cirith Ungol. Since Belzagar did not seem to understand your message of warning, Legolas has advised you to write the warning yourself in Belzagar's book.\n3\tTalk to Legolas in the Tower of Cirith Ungol\tLegolas can be found in the turret of the Tower of Cirith Ungol. You have delivered the message of warning to Belzagar and written it as such in his book. You should now speak to Legolas.\n",
})
